###Mapping
// ============================================================
// product_catalogue::Mapping
// ============================================================
// It INCLUDES both dependencies' mappings, which is what makes three different kinds of
// cross-project reference below resolvable at once:
//
//  * `extends [pprPricedProduct]` and `extends [pprAutocall]` -- set ids that live in
//    product-pricing. Extending is what makes the catalogue sets short rather than enormous:
//    the primary key, the main table CI_INSTRUMENT and every inherited column mapping come
//    from the set being extended, across THREE project boundaries
//    (pct -> ppr -> prd -> ci).
//  * `dataset[sdiDataset]`, `publication[sdiPublication]`, `consumer[sdiConsumer]`,
//    `acknowledgement[sdiAck]` -- property mappings whose TARGET set id lives in
//    static-distribution. Note `sdiAck`, not `sdiAcknowledgement`.
//  * `pricingRun[pprPricingRun]` -- the same, into product-pricing.
//
// Both dependencies name every set id explicitly, so there is no `product_pricing_
// PprPricedProduct` or `static_distribution_SdiAcknowledgement` default to fall back on, and
// every id below is taken from the dependency's MANIFEST (or, for product-pricing, from its
// mapping) rather than guessed.
//
// core_instrument::Mapping arrives twice -- through product_core (via product_pricing) and
// through reference_data (via static_distribution). A diamond include is fine and resolves
// to one. Do NOT include either of them, or product_core::Mapping, a second time: they are
// not declared dependencies of this project.
//
// Three shape facts, stated once here rather than inferred from four hundred lines below:
//
//  * The main table of every catalogue-product set is core-instrument's CI_INSTRUMENT, three
//    projects up. This project's own columns live in pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY and are reached
//    through Pct_EntryInstrument, so a property mapping reads
//    `[product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.COL` and a
//    two-hop one reads `@Pct_EntryInstrument > @Pct_EntryCatalogue`.
//  * Every set that adds a property declares it on its OWN set. A property declared on a
//    subclass cannot be mapped on the parent's set -- the trap product-core and
//    product-pricing both recorded, and the reason PctWithdrawnProduct's five columns are on
//    [pctWithdrawn] and not on [pctProduct].
//  * The two `~distinct` sets have NO table of their own and their `~primaryKey` names the
//    COLLAPSED column, never the source table's own key. Directive order is `~distinct`,
//    `~primaryKey`, `~mainTable`.
//
// No EnumerationMapping is needed: this project declares no enums, and the two enum-valued
// properties it inherits (assetClass, status from core-instrument; manufacturerCountry,
// settlementCurrency from product-core) are already transformed by the included mappings.
Mapping product_catalogue::Mapping
(
   include product_pricing::Mapping
   include static_distribution::Mapping

   // ================================================================================
   // 1. THE TWO ~DISTINCT SETS -- no table, one over ours, one over a dependency's
   // ================================================================================

   // The jurisdictions the catalogue is barred in anywhere. PCT_JURISDICTION_BAR is keyed on
   // (INSTRUMENT_ID, JURISDICTION_CODE), so keying this set that way would leave one row per
   // bar and the ~distinct would collapse nothing. Keyed on JURISDICTION_CODE alone, forty
   // products barred in one country become one row. JURISDICTION_NAME and
   // JURISDICTION_REGION are safe to map here because they are facts about the jurisdiction,
   // repeated identically on every bar row for it.
   *product_catalogue::PctBarredJurisdiction[pctBarredJurisdiction]: Relational
   {
      ~distinct
      ~primaryKey ( [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_JURISDICTION_BAR.JURISDICTION_CODE )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_JURISDICTION_BAR
      jurisdictionCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_JURISDICTION_BAR.JURISDICTION_CODE,
      jurisdictionName: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_JURISDICTION_BAR.JURISDICTION_NAME,
      jurisdictionRegion: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_JURISDICTION_BAR.JURISDICTION_REGION
   }

   // The pricing desks that manufacture anything at all -- collapsed across the project
   // boundary. PPR_PRODUCT_PRICING is keyed on INSTRUMENT_ID and stamps PRICING_DESK on
   // every product row, so the distinct values of that column ARE the manufacturing-desk
   // universe, and a desk pricing three hundred products is three hundred rows there and
   // one row here.
   *product_catalogue::PctManufacturingDesk[pctManufacturingDesk]: Relational
   {
      ~distinct
      ~primaryKey ( [product_pricing::Store]PPR_PRODUCT_PRICING.PRICING_DESK )
      ~mainTable [product_pricing::Store]PPR_PRODUCT_PRICING
      manufacturingDeskName: [product_pricing::Store]PPR_PRODUCT_PRICING.PRICING_DESK
   }

   // ================================================================================
   // 2. THE CATALOGUE OVERLAY -- extending product-pricing's sets
   // ================================================================================

   // The root of this project's overlay, and the point where it joins the dependency's
   // taxonomy. It adds no primary key and no main table -- both come from [pprPricedProduct],
   // which took them from [prdProduct], which took them from [ciBase] -- only the join to
   // this project's overlay table and the filter that says the entry has been published.
   product_catalogue::PctCatalogueProduct[pctProduct] extends [pprPricedProduct]: Relational
   {
      ~filter [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | [product_catalogue::Store]PctListedRows
      salesStatus: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.SALES_STATUS,
      catalogueCode: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.CATALOGUE_CODE,
      salesName: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.SALES_NAME,
      salesHeadline: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.SALES_HEADLINE,
      primaryChannelCode: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.PRIMARY_CHANNEL_CODE,
      salesDeskCode: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.SALES_DESK_CODE,
      targetMarketCode: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.TARGET_MARKET_CODE,
      strategyCode: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.STRATEGY_CODE,
      trainingCode: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.TRAINING_CODE,
      salesWrapper: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.SALES_WRAPPER,
      minimumTicketAmount: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.MIN_TICKET_AMOUNT,
      minimumTicketCurrency: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.MIN_TICKET_CURRENCY,
      listedOn: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.LISTED_ON,
      deListedOn: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.DE_LISTED_ON,
      isFeatured: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.IS_FEATURED,
      salesRank: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.SALES_RANK,
      documentPackCode: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.DOCUMENT_PACK_CODE,
      catalogue[pctCatalogue]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument > @Pct_EntryCatalogue,
      channel[pctChannel]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument > @Pct_EntryChannel,
      salesDesk[pctSalesDesk]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument > @Pct_EntryDesk,
      targetMarketProfile[pctTargetMarket]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument > @Pct_EntryTargetMarket,
      distributionStrategy[pctStrategy]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument > @Pct_EntryStrategy,
      requiredTraining[pctTraining]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument > @Pct_EntryTraining,
      categoryEligibilities[pctEligibility]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_InstrumentEligibility,
      jurisdictionBars[pctJurisdictionBar]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_InstrumentBar,
      documentRequirements[pctDocRequirement]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_InstrumentDocRequirement,
      documents[pctDocument]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_InstrumentDocument,
      salesRestrictions[pctRestriction]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_InstrumentRestriction,
      indicativePrices[pctIndicativePrice]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_InstrumentIndicativePrice,
      commissionTerms[pctCommission]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_InstrumentCommission
   }

   // ---- the four sales statuses, on this project's own SALES_STATUS column ----
   // Each extends [pctProduct], so the chain to the base is five links long:
   // status -> pctProduct -> pprPricedProduct -> prdProduct -> ciBase, crossing a project
   // boundary three times.

   product_catalogue::PctOfferableProduct[pctOfferable] extends [pctProduct]: Relational
   {
      ~filter [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | [product_catalogue::Store]PctOfferableRows
      offerableFrom: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.OFFERABLE_FROM,
      maximumTicketAmount: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.MAX_TICKET_AMOUNT,
      hasOnlineFactsheet: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.HAS_ONLINE_FACTSHEET,
      quoteTurnaroundMinutes: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.QUOTE_TURNAROUND_MINUTES,
      isSelfServiceEligible: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.IS_SELF_SERVICE
   }

   product_catalogue::PctRestrictedProduct[pctRestricted] extends [pctProduct]: Relational
   {
      ~filter [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | [product_catalogue::Store]PctRestrictedRows
      restrictionReason: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.RESTRICTION_REASON,
      approverRole: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.APPROVER_ROLE,
      needsSecondSignoff: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.NEEDS_SECOND_SIGNOFF,
      restrictionReviewOn: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.RESTRICTION_REVIEW_ON,
      maxClientsPerMonth: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.MAX_CLIENTS_PER_MONTH
   }

   // The population this project exists to keep visible: no longer offered, still held.
   product_catalogue::PctWithdrawnProduct[pctWithdrawn] extends [pctProduct]: Relational
   {
      ~filter [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | [product_catalogue::Store]PctWithdrawnRows
      withdrawnReason: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.WITHDRAWN_REASON,
      holdingsMayContinue: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.HOLDINGS_MAY_CONTINUE,
      lastTradeOn: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.LAST_TRADE_ON,
      runoffEndOn: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.RUNOFF_END_ON,
      successorProductCode: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.SUCCESSOR_PRODUCT_CODE
   }

   product_catalogue::PctPipelineProduct[pctPipeline] extends [pctProduct]: Relational
   {
      ~filter [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | [product_catalogue::Store]PctPipelineRows
      pipelineStage: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.PIPELINE_STAGE,
      expectedLaunchOn: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.EXPECTED_LAUNCH_ON,
      sponsorDesk: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.SPONSOR_DESK,
      launchBlocker: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.LAUNCH_BLOCKER,
      pilotClientCount: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.PILOT_CLIENT_COUNT
   }

   // ---- one concrete payoff, extending product-pricing's own concrete set ----
   // This does not extend [pctProduct]; it extends [pprAutocall], because the facts it adds
   // are facts about that payoff. Its filter is on SALES_WRAPPER rather than SALES_STATUS,
   // precisely because it is on a different branch and must not be cut by the same column
   // twice.
   product_catalogue::PctCataloguedAutocall[pctAutocall] extends [pprAutocall]: Relational
   {
      ~filter [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | [product_catalogue::Store]PctAutocallWrapperRows
      salesPitchSummary: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.SALES_PITCH_SUMMARY,
      couponDisplayPercent: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.COUPON_DISPLAY_PCT,
      isCapitalAtRiskFlagged: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.IS_CAPITAL_AT_RISK_FLAGGED,
      illustrationScenarioCount: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.ILLUSTRATION_SCENARIO_COUNT,
      requiresRiskWarningCall: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EntryInstrument | pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_ENTRY.REQUIRES_RISK_WARNING_CALL
   }

   // ================================================================================
   // 3. THE CATALOGUE ITSELF -- our own tables in the `pct` SCHEMA
   //    every reference is [product_catalogue::Store]pct.TABLE.COLUMN
   // ================================================================================

   *product_catalogue::PctCatalogue[pctCatalogue]: Relational
   {
      ~primaryKey ( [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE.CATALOGUE_CODE )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE
      catalogueCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE.CATALOGUE_CODE,
      catalogueName: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE.CATALOGUE_NAME,
      edition: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE.EDITION,
      regionCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE.REGION_CODE,
      audience: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE.AUDIENCE,
      ownerDesk: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE.OWNER_DESK,
      datasetCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE.DATASET_CODE,
      retiredOn: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE.RETIRED_ON,
      versions[pctVersion]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_CatalogueVersion,
      dataset[sdiDataset]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_CatalogueDataset
   }

   *product_catalogue::PctCatalogueVersion[pctVersion]: Relational
   {
      ~primaryKey ( [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.VERSION_ID )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION
      versionId: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.VERSION_ID,
      catalogueCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.CATALOGUE_CODE,
      versionNumber: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.VERSION_NUMBER,
      publishedOn: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.PUBLISHED_ON,
      publicationId: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.PUBLICATION_ID,
      entryCount: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.ENTRY_COUNT,
      withdrawnCount: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.WITHDRAWN_COUNT,
      approvedBy: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.APPROVED_BY,
      supersededOn: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_VERSION.SUPERSEDED_ON,
      catalogue[pctCatalogue]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_CatalogueVersion,
      lines[pctLine]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_LineVersion,
      publication[sdiPublication]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_VersionPublication,
      distributions[pctDistribution]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_DistributionVersion
   }

   *product_catalogue::PctCatalogueLine[pctLine]: Relational
   {
      ~primaryKey
      (
         [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.VERSION_ID,
         [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.INSTRUMENT_ID
      )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE
      versionId: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.VERSION_ID,
      instrumentId: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.INSTRUMENT_ID,
      pagePosition: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.POSITION_NUMBER,
      headline: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.HEADLINE,
      printedOfferPrice: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.PRINTED_OFFER_PRICE,
      isNewThisEdition: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.IS_NEW_THIS_EDITION,
      isHighlighted: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.IS_HIGHLIGHTED,
      removalNote: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATALOGUE_LINE.REMOVAL_NOTE,
      version[pctVersion]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_LineVersion,
      product[pctProduct]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_InstrumentLine
   }

   // The two static-distribution property mappings that make the catalogue a DISTRIBUTED
   // document rather than a stored one: the consumer it went to, and the acknowledgement row
   // whose acknowledgedAt is null until that consumer fills it in.
   *product_catalogue::PctCatalogueDistribution[pctDistribution]: Relational
   {
      ~primaryKey
      (
         [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION.VERSION_ID,
         [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION.CONSUMER_ID
      )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION
      versionId: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION.VERSION_ID,
      consumerId: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION.CONSUMER_ID,
      publicationId: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION.PUBLICATION_ID,
      sentAt: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION.SENT_AT,
      deliveryFormat: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION.DELIVERY_FORMAT,
      recipientCount: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION.RECIPIENT_COUNT,
      failureCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_DISTRIBUTION.FAILURE_CODE,
      version[pctVersion]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_DistributionVersion,
      consumer[sdiConsumer]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_DistributionConsumer,
      acknowledgement[sdiAck]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_DistributionAck
   }

   // ================================================================================
   // 4. WHO MAY BE SOLD WHAT
   // ================================================================================

   *product_catalogue::PctSalesChannel[pctChannel]: Relational
   {
      ~primaryKey ( [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CHANNEL.CHANNEL_CODE )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CHANNEL
      channelCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CHANNEL.CHANNEL_CODE,
      channelName: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CHANNEL.CHANNEL_NAME,
      channelKind: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CHANNEL.CHANNEL_KIND,
      isAdvised: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CHANNEL.IS_ADVISED,
      needsSuitabilityTest: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CHANNEL.NEEDS_SUITABILITY_TEST,
      minimumClientAssets: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CHANNEL.MIN_CLIENT_ASSETS,
      retiredOn: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CHANNEL.RETIRED_ON
   }

   // `manufacturer` targets the ~distinct set whose main table is product-pricing's
   // PPR_PRODUCT_PRICING: a sales desk faces a manufacturing desk that exists because some
   // product is priced by it.
   *product_catalogue::PctSalesDesk[pctSalesDesk]: Relational
   {
      ~primaryKey ( [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK.DESK_CODE )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK
      deskCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK.DESK_CODE,
      deskName: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK.DESK_NAME,
      regionCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK.REGION_CODE,
      jurisdictionCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK.JURISDICTION_CODE,
      manufacturingDeskName: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK.MANUFACTURING_DESK,
      headOfDesk: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK.HEAD_OF_DESK,
      headcount: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK.HEADCOUNT,
      closedOn: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_SALES_DESK.CLOSED_ON,
      manufacturer[pctManufacturingDesk]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_DeskManufacturer
   }

   *product_catalogue::PctClientCategory[pctClientCategory]: Relational
   {
      ~primaryKey ( [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CLIENT_CATEGORY.CATEGORY_CODE )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CLIENT_CATEGORY
      categoryCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CLIENT_CATEGORY.CATEGORY_CODE,
      categoryName: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CLIENT_CATEGORY.CATEGORY_NAME,
      regulatoryBasis: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CLIENT_CATEGORY.REGULATORY_BASIS,
      needsAppropriatenessTest: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CLIENT_CATEGORY.NEEDS_APPROPRIATENESS_TEST,
      needsSuitabilityReport: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CLIENT_CATEGORY.NEEDS_SUITABILITY_REPORT,
      maxComplexityScore: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CLIENT_CATEGORY.MAX_COMPLEXITY_SCORE,
      eligibilities[pctEligibility]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EligibilityCategory
   }

   *product_catalogue::PctCategoryEligibility[pctEligibility]: Relational
   {
      ~primaryKey
      (
         [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY.INSTRUMENT_ID,
         [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY.CATEGORY_CODE
      )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY
      instrumentId: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY.INSTRUMENT_ID,
      categoryCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY.CATEGORY_CODE,
      eligibilityStatus: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY.ELIGIBILITY_STATUS,
      rationale: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY.RATIONALE,
      assessedOn: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY.ASSESSED_ON,
      reviewDueOn: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY.REVIEW_DUE_ON,
      approvedBy: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_CATEGORY_ELIGIBILITY.APPROVED_BY,
      category[pctClientCategory]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_EligibilityCategory,
      product[pctProduct]: [product_catalogue::Store]@Pct_InstrumentEligibility
   }

   *product_catalogue::PctTargetMarket[pctTargetMarket]: Relational
   {
      ~primaryKey ( [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_TARGET_MARKET.TARGET_MARKET_CODE )
      ~mainTable [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_TARGET_MARKET
      targetMarketCode: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_TARGET_MARKET.TARGET_MARKET_CODE,
      investorType: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_TARGET_MARKET.INVESTOR_TYPE,
      knowledgeLevel: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_TARGET_MARKET.KNOWLEDGE_LEVEL,
      riskTolerance: [product_catalogue::Store]pct.PCT_TARGET_MARKET.RISK_TOLERANCE,
